    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> 10:04AM EDT</p><h2>LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_clarity/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Diffuse attenuation coefficient for PAR (m^-1), FIXED absolute scale <b>LOWEST 0.016</b> clearest (dark blue) → 0.5 → <b>1.0</b> turbid (red) → 1.5 → <b>HIGHEST+ 2</b> most turbid (deep purple). Larger values always mean murkier water; source values are never altered.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP VIIRS Kd(PAR) diffuse attenuation, Global 4 km, Daily (ERDDAP; newest-wins across nesdisVHNkdparDaily NRT and nesdisVHNSQkdparDaily Science Quality, per-day fallback)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
